hanical ventilation. Am J Respir Crit Care Med. 2007;175:935–942. doi: 10.1164/rccm.200609-1322OC. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 89. Schuierer L., Gebhard M., Ruf H.G., Jaschinski U., Berghaus T.M., Wittmann M., et al. Impact of acyclovir use on survival of patients with ventilator-associated pneumonia and high load herpes simplex virus replication. Crit Care. 2020;24:12. doi: 10.1186/s13054-019-2701-5. PMID: 31924246; PMCID: PMC6954562. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 90. Xu R., Zhou Y., Cai L., Wang L., Han J., Yang X., et al. Co-reactivation of human herpesvirus alpha subfamily (HSV 1 and VZV) in critically ill patients with COVID-19. Br J Dermatol. 2020;183:1145–1147. doi: 10.1111/bjd.19484. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 91. Le Balc’h P., Pinceaux K., Pronier C., Seguin P., Tadié J.M., Reizine F. Herpes simplex virus and cytomegalovirus reactivations among severe COVID-19 patients. Crit Care. 2020;24:530. doi: 10.1186/s13054-020-03252-3. PMID: 32859241; PMCID: PMC7453668. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 92. Busani S., Bedini A., Biagioni E., Serio L., Tonelli R., Meschiari M., et al. Two fatal cases of acute liver failure due to HSV-1 infection in COVID-19 patients following immunomodulatory therapies. Clin Infect Dis. 2020 doi: 10.1093/cid/ciaa1246. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 93. Carll W.C., Rady M.Y., Salomao M.A., Patel B., Singh V.P., Sen A. Cytomegalovirus haemorrhagic enterocolitis associated with severe infection with COVID-19. BMJ Open Gastroenterol. 2021;8 doi: 10.1136/bmjgast-2020-000556. PMID: 33436481; PMCID: PMC7804824. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Associated Data This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article. Supplementary Materials mmc1.pdf (37.4KB, pdf) mmc2.pdf (44.7KB, pdf) mmc3.doc (25KB, doc)',14028,'2025-10-15 11:0