INSERT INTO corpus VALUES(5340,'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7095239','The role of blood microfilters in clinical practice.','Kapadia F, Valentine S, Smith G.','1992','microaggregate nhftr leucocyte alloimmunisation microfiltration microaggregate microaggregates leucocyte eckert microembolism intensivther notfallmed buley lumley microfilters wenz microaggregate wenz microfiltration superfluous vox tb04846 microaggregates worl microaggregates tb08988 derrington tb10786 cpo doughty maclennan mcclelland dbl prowse macroaggregate vox tb01120 reul beal reul lefrak wenz gurtlinger dugan microaggregate simlified vox tb01872 isoantigenic incompatability leucocytes vox tb04256 mollison butcher parravicini rebulla apuzzo wenz sirchia leucocyte meryman hornblower leucocytes robb mongulis jalo microembolism endotoxic barret litwin microembolisms dhurandhur litwin microembolism swank microemboli monnucci federici sirchia vox tb01080 boughton bareford vox tb03046 bareford hawker boughton sequestration tb02323 bareford macwhannel lanchbury boughton asplenic vox tb05024 opsonic reticuloendothelial mosher hezzey golenwsky s191 mosher hezzey golenwsky scovill blumenstock opsonic frewin beal frewin beilby haylock beal microfiltration vox tb03025 dumbar cannarella microaggregate haemaglobin langhurst gooch castello microaggregate tomassini micropore linko microaggregate mezzey mones microaggregate yellon vernick golub dalmasso vox tb01916 meryman alloimmunisation leucocyte s0887 tartter verdonck graan hentzen yce mudde gast neukocyte graan hentzen yce gratama mudde loon verdonck willemze gast leucocyte hardiman lister leucocyte tb02473 hodson leucocytes graan hentzen yce gast gratama verdonck mudde graan hentzen yce gratama mudde verdonck houbiers jga sebens loon willemze gast haematologic intensine sayers cays 42nd aabb eernisse refractoriness schiffer dutcher aisner hogge wiernik alloimmunisation tb02965 sniecinski nowicki refractoriness alloimmunisation andreu dewailly leberre quarre bidet tardivel devers soreall boccaccio piard bidet genetet faunchet leucocyte concentrates claas fhj voogt wasser mnjm eernisse alloimmunisation vox tb03892 myllyla ruutu oksanen kekomaki rasi congr saarinen kekomaki siimes myllyla refractoriness multitransfused leucocyte','Abstract Blood filters have been available since the 1930s. In this review we evaluate the role of microaggregate filters (MF) in certain transfusion complications, namely non-haemolytic febrile transfusion reactions (NHFTR), pulmonary injury, thrombocytopenia, fibronectin depletion and histamine release. We review the latest generation of leucocyte depleting filters and discuss their role in preventing alloimmunisation, immunosuppression and CMV transmission. Finally, we provide a rationale for the role of blood microfiltration in the present day practice of intensive care medicine. Key words: Microaggregate blood filters, Microaggregates, Leucocyte-depleting filters References 1. Eckert G. Prevention of pulmonary microembolism during blood transfusion by means of fine mesh filters. Anaesthesia. Intensivther Notfallmed. 1980;15:201–206. [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 2. Buley R, Lumley J. Some observations on blood microfilters. Ann Coll Surg Engl. 1975;57:262–267. [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 3. Wenz B. Microaggregate blood filtration and the febrile transfusion reaction. Transfusion. 1983;23:95–98. doi: 10.1046/j.1537-2995.1983.23283172868.x. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 4. Wenz B. When is microfiltration of whole blood and red cell concentrate essential? When is it superfluous. Int Forum Vox Sang. 1986;50:63–64. doi: 10.1111/j.1423-0410.1986.tb04846.x. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 5. Lloyd GM, Marshall L. Blood microaggregates, their role in transfusion reactions. Intensive Care Worl. 1986;3:119–122. [ Google Scholar ] 6. Bolton DT, Peeters A. Microaggregates and filtration. Correspondence. Anaesthesia. 1988;43:330–331. doi: 10.1111/j.1365-2044.1988.tb08988.x. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 7. Derrington C. The present status of blood filtration. Anaesthesia. 1985;40:334–347. doi: 10.1111/j.1365-2044.1985.tb10786.x. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 8. Wright G. ACO and CPO blood preservation. Lancet. 1974;II:173. doi: 10.1016/s0140-6736(74)91613-4. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 9. Wright G (1975) The causes and effects of blood cell aggregates. International Symposium on the Fine Screen Filtration of Stored Blood, pp 21–32 10. Lowe GD. Filtration in IV therapy. A review of the clinical and technical aspects of intravenous fluid and blood filtration, in four parts. Part III: Clinical aspects of blood filtration. Br J IV Ther. 1981;2:28–38. [ Google Scholar ] 11. Robertson M, Boulton F, Doughty R, MacLennan JR, Collins A, McClelland DBL, Prowse CV. Macroaggregate formation in optimal additive red cells. Vox Sang. 1985;49:259–266. doi: 10.1111/j.1423-0410.1985.tb01120.x. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 12. Reul GJ, Beal AC, Greenberg S. Protection of the pulmonary vasculature by fine screen blood filtration. Chest. 1974;66:4–9. doi: 10.1378/chest.66.1.4. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 13. Reul GJ, Greenberg SD, Lefrak EA. Prevention of post traumatic pulmonary insufficiency fine screen filtration of blood. Arch Surg. 1973;106:386–394. doi: 10.1001/archsurg.1973.01350160008002. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 14. Wenz B, Gurtlinger KF, O''Toole AM, Dugan EP. Preparation of granulocyte poor red blood cells by microaggregate filtration: a simlified method to minimise future transfusion reactions. Vox Sang. 1980;39:282–287. doi: 10.1111/j.1423-0410.1980.tb01872.x. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 15. Perkins HA, Payne R, Ferguson J, Wood M. Non haemolytic febrile transfusion reactions. Quantitative effect of blood components with emphasis on isoantigenic incompatability of leucocytes. Vox Sang. 1966;11:578–600. doi: 10.1111/j.1423-0410.1966.tb04256.x. [ DOI ] [ Pu